// microbench closure: the whole TagClass subtree under a TagClass, root included (follow
// isSubclassOf backwards, child -> parent edges read from the parent side, to any depth).
// Reads: the isSubclassOf _to edge index of every class in the subtree; returns each class's
// _key only.
// Evaluator: queries/nhop.py closure -- read_closure(isSubclassOf, in) level by level until no
// new class; final = the class set, root included, one row per class.
// mb2 lineage: none (the IC12 tag-hierarchy walk). The depth bound 100 stands for "unbounded":
// the LDBC TagClass hierarchy is a handful of levels deep.
FOR c IN 0..100 INBOUND CONCAT("TagClass/", @tagClassId) isSubclassOf
    OPTIONS {order: "bfs", uniqueVertices: "global"}
    RETURN c._key
